      "text": "I want to be fully transparent with you about what my research has found — and what it hasn't.\n\n---\n\n## What I Can Confirm\n\nMy searches and tool calls did confirm the following **bibliographic details** about the book:\n\n| Field | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| **Title** | *Molecular Biology of the Cell*, 7th Edition |\n| **Authors** | Bruce Alberts, Rebecca Heald, Alexander Johnson, David Morgan, Martin Raff, Keith Roberts, Peter Walter |\n| **Publisher** | W. W. Norton & Company |\n| **Year** | 2022 |\n| **ISBN** | 978-0-393-88423-5 (one variant listed) |\n| **Key new features** | Updates on cryo-EM, single-molecule techniques, and genome editing (CRISPR) |\n\n---\n\n## What I Was Unable to Retrieve\n\nDespite multiple searches and attempts to fetch the publisher's page, Wikipedia's chapter list, and other sources, **I was not able to retrieve a verified, chapter-by-chapter table of contents** for the 7th edition. The pages either returned only high-level summaries or could not be accessed. I won't fabricate a chapter list, as that could mislead your syllabus planning.\n\n---\n\n## What I Recommend Instead\n\nHere are the most reliable ways to get the exact 7th-edition chapter listing:\n\n1. **Publisher's website directly:**\n[https://wwnorton.com/books/molecular-biology-of-the-cell](https://wwnorton.com/books/molecular-biology-of-the-cell) — W. W. Norton typically posts a full TOC on the book's product page.\n\n2. **Google Books preview:**\nSearch \"Molecular Biology of the Cell 7th edition\" on [books.google.com](https://books.google.com) — previews often include the table of contents pages.\n\n3. **Your institutional library catalog** (e.g., WorldCat or your university's system) — many catalog entries include the full TOC.\n\n4. **Amazon's \"Look Inside\" feature** — searching the ISBN `978-0-393-88423-5` on Amazon often reveals the TOC in the preview.\n\nI'm sorry I couldn't pull the full chapter list directly — but I wanted to give you accurate information rather than risk putting incorrect chapter titles on your syllabus.",
